We need to change Auto Recorder functionality  and need to use a Local(client side and not server side) Headless Execution architecture.
Follow instructions carefully and keep implementation clean, minimal, and robust.

## ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
* Execution happens on user/client machine via Local Agent.
* Backend (ECS) orchestrates execution.
* Frontend UI shows snapshot preview same like currently what we have but now snapshot will come from user machine and not server.
* Browser remains headless (hidden) always for all users.
* Admin-only debug mode can enable visible browser (keep a comment in code to implement this later, as of now will go defualt hidden for all)

1. LOCAL AGENT

Create a lightweight agent (Python → packaged as executable):
User downloads → double-click → agent runs (no install, no admin rights)
Responsibilities:
1. Run local HTTP server:
   GET http://localhost:4789/health → returns "OK"
2. Accept session registration:
   POST /register?sessionId=<id>
3. Maintain active sessionId
4. Connect to backend via WebSocket:
   /ws/local-agent
5. Send:
   {
   "type": "AGENT_REGISTER",
   "sessionId": "<id>"
   }

2. BROWSER EXECUTION (LOCAL)
Agent launches Chrome:
Default (hidden):
* --headless=new
* --remote-debugging-port=9222
* --no-sandbox
* --disable-gpu

Agent must:
* Connect via CDP
* Reuse existing execution logic (click, type, navigate)

3. SNAPSHOT STREAMING
After key actions of step execution and page loading, agent Captures the snapshot and send to backend which will get diplahyed on frontend

4. SESSION MANAGEMENT

Frontend:
* Generate UUID per session
Flow:
1. User clicks "Start Recording"
2. Generate sessionId
3. Call:
   http://localhost:4789/register?sessionId=<id>
Agent:
* Stores sessionId
* Registers via WebSocket
Backend:
* Maintain mapping:
  sessionId → agent connection
All commands routed via sessionId

5. AGENT DETECTION
Frontend must:
1. Call:
   http://localhost:4789/health
2. If fail:
   Show modal when user clicks on auto recorder tab. Modal should be non closable and show message like:
   "PerfSonic Agent is required to use the recorder functionality"
   Buttons:
   * Download Agent (put one Important line at modal bottom, "Once downloaded, Please double click Agent.exe to start"
   * Retry
3. Retry detection every 2–3 seconds
4. Once detected → remove modal and on top right show Agent connected with green dot heartbeat, until agent is responding.

on every user machine we need to restart agent once their machine gets restared-
Startup Folder (Simplest & Safe)-
Add shortcut to:
C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs\Startup

How agent does it (on first run):
creates .lnk shortcut of itself
places in startup folder

---

6. EXECUTION FLOW
Backend remains same:
* Receives steps
* Uses existing logic:
  * login handling
  * form handling
  * navigation
  * ambiguity handling

BUT:
* Instead of server browser → send commands to agent

7. HEARTBEAT & FAILURE HANDLING
Agent:
* Send heartbeat every few seconds
Backend:
* If heartbeat lost:
  Pause execution
  Notify frontend:
  "Agent disconnected"
Handle:
* browser crash
* agent shutdown
* network loss

8. RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
On session end:
Agent must:
* Close browser
* Release CDP connection
* Clear sessionId

Backend must:
* Remove session mapping

9. UI REQUIREMENTS

Entire frontend should be as it is, now just logs and snapshot will come via agent from user machine. Show one line at bottom- 
"Flow navigation runs locally on user machine"

10. SECURITY & TRANSPARENCY
* Store username/password, form data everything local to user only in user machine cache.
* Do NOT embed browser in UI
* Do NOT use Chrome extensions
* Do NOT move execution back to server

## GOAL

Provide a seamless experience:
User clicks "Start Recording"
→ Local agent runs hidden browser
→ Backend controls execution
→ UI shows preview
→ Works for all enterprise apps (cert/VPN included)

